{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-6:137\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Here دين is the religious allegiance that partners distort; beside مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ, it raises the question of whose authority defines the dīn people claim.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"6:137\",\"ar\":\"وَلِيَلْبِسُوا۟ عَلَيْهِمْ دِينَهُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus also names dīn under divine ownership.\",\"limits\":\"This passage does not place the distortion on a reckoning day or describe its judgment.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-6:158\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The day in 6:158 is a threshold after which new faith or good earned in faith cannot benefit a soul; it gives يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ an irreversible moral horizon.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"6:158\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَ يَأْتِى بَعْضُ ءَايَٰتِ رَبِّكَ لَا يَنفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَٰنُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ ءَامَنَتْ مِن قَبْلُ أَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِىٓ إِيمَٰنِهَا خَيْرًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus pairs a named day with dīn, while this passage specifies a day when faith and deeds face a final limit.\",\"limits\":\"The verse describes the arrival of some of the Lord’s signs; it does not call this event يوم الدين or describe a full accounting.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-6:159\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The divided دينهم is followed by the people’s affair returning to Allah and His telling them what they did; the focus can thus be heard against human division of dīn and divine final report.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"6:159\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُوا۟ دِينَهُمْ وَكَانُوا۟ شِيَعًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"6:159\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّمَآ أَمْرُهُمْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَفْعَلُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages place دين in relation to Allah, and 6:159 explicitly joins it to a report of deeds.\",\"limits\":\"The verse gives no date for the report and does not use the focus’s day formula.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-6:161\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The description دينًا قيمًا presents dīn as an upright religious way; that Quranic use could keep an order or way sense in hearing the focus’s dīn.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"6:161\",\"ar\":\"دِينًۭا قِيَمًۭا مِّلَّةَ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ حَنِيفًۭا\"}],\"missing\":\"This verse does not pair dīn with a day or reckoning. A dictionary sense or Quranic use of يوم الدين that retains the upright-way sense could establish whether that layer belongs in the focus.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:8\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The weighing on that day is called الحق, and heavy scales lead to success; this supplies a measure-of-deeds scene for the focus’s Day.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:8\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْوَزْنُ يَوْمَئِذٍ ٱلْحَقُّ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:8\",\"ar\":\"فَمَن ثَقُلَتْ مَوَٰزِينُهُۥ فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْمُفْلِحُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names a day of dīn, and this passage explicitly sets truthful weighing on that day.\",\"limits\":\"The focus gives no scale or weight imagery itself.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:9\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Light scales bring loss of the self, giving the weighing scene’s adverse outcome alongside the focus’s divine ownership of the Day.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:9\",\"ar\":\"وَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَٰزِينُهُۥ فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ خَسِرُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَهُم\"}],\"activation\":\"The preceding 7:8 places this opposite result within the same weighing on that day.\",\"limits\":\"This verse describes one outcome and does not itself name the owner of the Day.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:14\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Iblis asks for time until the day people are raised; the Day in the focus can also be heard as the limit of a deferred span.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:14\",\"ar\":\"أَنظِرْنِىٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s يَوْمِ is a definite event horizon, and this request names resurrection as an endpoint.\",\"limits\":\"Iblis asks to survive until that day; the verse does not describe his reckoning or outcome there.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:29\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The command to call on Allah with dīn made sincere is followed by the reminder that people return as He began them; present devotion is set beside return to Allah.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:29\",\"ar\":\"وَٱدْعُوهُ مُخْلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ ۚ كَمَا بَدَأَكُمْ تَعُودُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse joins the same dīn root to worship and immediately names a return, activating both dimensions of the focus.\",\"limits\":\"It does not say that the return is specifically called يوم الدين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:51\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Those who made their dīn play are met with divine neglect on the day they forgot to meet; the passage binds present treatment of dīn to the final meeting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:51\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُوا۟ دِينَهُمْ لَهْوًۭا وَلَعِبًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"7:51\",\"ar\":\"فَٱلْيَوْمَ نَنسَىٰهُمْ كَمَا نَسُوا۟ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِهِمْ هَٰذَا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s paired words يوم and الدين recur here across present conduct and the forgotten meeting.\",\"limits\":\"The passage describes a particular group’s consequence; it does not define every sense of dīn in the focus.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-7:158\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The formula gives Allah the ملك of the heavens and earth and links it to giving life and death; it broadens the focus’s ownership title to the whole life-and-death domain.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:158\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِى لَهُۥ مُلْكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:158\",\"ar\":\"يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ\"}],\"activation\":\"مَٰلِكِ in the focus and مُلْكُ here share the sovereignty root, while life and death lead toward the Day named there.\",\"limits\":\"This passage does not mention a judgment day or the accounting of deeds.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-8:72\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The phrase فِى ٱلدِّينِ makes aid an obligation within shared religious allegiance, illustrating a communal use of dīn beside the focus’s day-of-reckoning use.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"8:72\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنِ ٱسْتَنصَرُوكُمْ فِى ٱلدِّينِ فَعَلَيْكُمُ ٱلنَّصْرُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The shared dīn root opens a contrast between present communal bonds and the focus’s final horizon.\",\"limits\":\"This wartime covenant passage says nothing about a day of account.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-9:11\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Repentance, prayer, and almsgiving mark people as brothers in dīn, giving the word a present communal and ritual register alongside its use in the focus.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"9:11\",\"ar\":\"فَإِن تَابُوا۟ وَأَقَامُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُا۟ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَإِخْوَٰنُكُمْ فِى ٱلدِّينِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s dīn is also the root word naming this shared religious bond.\",\"limits\":\"The verse identifies community membership, not judgment on the Day.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-9:29\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Belief in the Last Day is set beside whether people يَدِينُونَ دِينَ الْحَقِّ; the passage places final-day belief and lived allegiance in one description.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"9:29\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا بِٱلْيَوْمِ ٱلْءَاخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُونَ مَا حَرَّمَ ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥ وَلَا يَدِينُونَ دِينَ ٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus likewise brings a day and dīn together, while this verse coordinates the Last Day with dīn al-haqq.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not state that dīn al-haqq and يوم الدين are the same expression or explain their causal relation.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-9:36\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The passage calls Allah’s sacred-month order ٱلدِّينُ ٱلْقَيِّمُ and locates it in a calendar grounded at creation; it may let the focus’s day resonate with divinely set temporal order.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"9:36\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ عِدَّةَ ٱلشُّهُورِ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ ٱثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًۭا فِى كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ\"},{\"ref\":\"9:36\",\"ar\":\"ذَٰلِكَ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلْقَيِّمُ\"}],\"missing\":\"The verse calls a calendar rule dīn, but does not connect that rule to يوم الدين. A lexical source or another passage joining divine time-order to the day-of-dīn formula could decide whether the temporal layer carries over.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-9:116\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Allah’s ملك over heavens and earth is paired with giving life and death, extending the focus’s ownership horizon across the conditions that precede judgment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"9:116\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَهُۥ مُلْكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"9:116\",\"ar\":\"يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The root shared by the focus’s مَٰلِكِ and this ملك formula activates the sovereignty link.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not describe resurrection or accounting after death.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:22\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"People call on Allah with dīn made sincere in a storm, promise gratitude, then after rescue transgress before the return and report in 10:23; the focus’s dīn stands against this gap between crisis devotion and conduct.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"10:22\",\"ar\":\"دَعَوُا۟ ٱللَّهَ مُخْلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ لَئِنْ أَنجَيْتَنَا مِنْ هَٰذِهِۦ لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"10:23\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ إِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَنُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names Allah as owner of dīn’s Day; this adjacent sequence puts sincere dīn, later acts, and return to Allah together.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not use يوم الدين or say the storm itself is a judgment scene.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:104\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The speaker identifies his dīn with worship of Allah, whom the verse describes as taking the listeners in death; this joins present religious stance to mortality.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"10:104\",\"ar\":\"إِن كُنتُمْ فِى شَكٍّۢ مِّن دِينِى\"},{\"ref\":\"10:104\",\"ar\":\"أَعْبُدُ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِى يَتَوَفَّىٰكُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"Dīn and death occur together in a declaration about whom to worship, a life-before-death frame for the focus’s Day.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not describe resurrection or recompense after death.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-10:105\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The command to orient the face toward dīn as a ḥanīf defines dīn as a present direction of life, a possible counterpart to its future horizon in the focus.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"10:105\",\"ar\":\"وَأَنْ أَقِمْ وَجْهَكَ لِلدِّينِ حَنِيفًۭا وَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s final dīn shares its root with this directive for present allegiance.\",\"limits\":\"This command does not mention a day, death, or account.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:31\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Noah disclaims possession of Allah’s خزائن and affirms that Allah knows what lies within people; this could connect the focus’s ownership title to exclusive divine knowledge of persons.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"11:31\",\"ar\":\"وَلَآ أَقُولُ لَكُمْ عِندِى خَزَآئِنُ ٱللَّهِ وَلَآ أَعْلَمُ ٱلْغَيْبَ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:31\",\"ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ\"}],\"missing\":\"The exchange concerns Noah’s limits as a prophet and does not name judgment. A passage connecting Allah’s knowledge of hidden selves to their later account could establish the link to the focus.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:99\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The people carry a curse in this life and on the Day of Resurrection, giving the focus’s day an outcome that extends a community’s consequence across both horizons.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"11:99\",\"ar\":\"وَأُتْبِعُوا۟ فِى هَٰذِهِۦ لَعْنَةًۭ وَيَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:98\",\"ar\":\"يَقْدُمُ قَوْمَهُۥ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ فَأَوْرَدَهُمُ ٱلنَّارَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The preceding scene brings a people to the Fire on Resurrection Day, and this verse states their continuing curse.\",\"limits\":\"These verses depict a particular condemned people, not the full range of judgment.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:103\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The day is described as one for which all people are gathered and which is witnessed; the focus’s Day therefore has a collective and public dimension.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"11:103\",\"ar\":\"ذَٰلِكَ يَوْمٌۭ مَّجْمُوعٌۭ لَّهُ ٱلنَّاسُ وَذَٰلِكَ يَوْمٌۭ مَّشْهُودٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"11:103\",\"ar\":\"لِّمَنْ خَافَ عَذَابَ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages make the day central, and this one explicitly gathers humanity for it.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not use the focus’s dīn term or name the Day’s owner in this clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-11:105\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"On that day no soul speaks except by His permission, and people divide into wretched and fortunate; the scene makes sovereignty audible as control over speech and outcome.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"11:105\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَ يَأْتِ لَا تَكَلَّمُ نَفْسٌ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِۦ ۚ فَمِنْهُمْ شَقِىٌّۭ وَسَعِيدٌۭ\"}],\"activation\":\"This day’s restriction and sorting specify what divine mastery over the focus’s Day entails.\",\"limits\":\"The verse gives no weighing procedure or detailed account of deeds.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:40\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The verse says judgment belongs only to Allah, commands worship of Him alone, and calls this dīn upright; it directly joins divine حكم and religious dīn beside the focus’s title and the Fatiha’s next line of exclusive worship.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"12:40\",\"ar\":\"إِنِ ٱلْحُكْمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:40\",\"ar\":\"أَمَرَ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوٓا۟ إِلَّآ إِيَّاهُ\"},{\"ref\":\"12:40\",\"ar\":\"ذَٰلِكَ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلْقَيِّمُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus ends its praise with dīn, and 1:5 immediately turns to exclusive worship, matching the sequence in 12:40.\",\"limits\":\"The Egyptian prison discourse names current judgment and worship, not specifically the final day or its accounting.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-12:92\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Here ٱلْيَوْمَ is Joseph’s immediate day of pardon; it shows that yawm alone can be ordinary and that the focus’s genitive ٱلدِّينِ supplies its eschatological specification.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"12:92\",\"ar\":\"لَا تَثْرِيبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْيَوْمَ ۖ يَغْفِرُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus also uses yawm, but qualifies it with dīn rather than the speaker’s immediate setting.\",\"limits\":\"Joseph’s pardon is a human reconciliation scene and does not describe final judgment.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-14:41\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Abraham asks forgiveness for himself, his parents, and believers on the day حساب stands; this makes the reckoning horizon a motive for communal petition, as the Fatiha moves from praise into request.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"14:41\",\"ar\":\"رَبَّنَا ٱغْفِرْ لِى وَلِوَٰلِدَىَّ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ يَوْمَ يَقُومُ ٱلْحِسَابُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The Fatiha places the focus’s Day just before a plural request, while Abraham’s prayer explicitly asks for forgiveness on the standing of حساب.\",\"limits\":\"The wording in 14:41 is يوم يقوم الحساب, not يوم الدين, and does not state the same grammatical relation.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-14:48\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The earth and heavens are changed and people appear before Allah, the One, the Subduer; the focus’s Day opens onto cosmic upheaval and exposure before sovereign power.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"14:48\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَ تُبَدَّلُ ٱلْأَرْضُ غَيْرَ ٱلْأَرْضِ وَٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:48\",\"ar\":\"وَبَرَزُوا۟ لِلَّهِ ٱلْوَٰحِدِ ٱلْقَهَّارِ\"},{\"ref\":\"14:49\",\"ar\":\"وَتَرَى ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ مُّقَرَّنِينَ فِى ٱلْأَصْفَادِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names Allah as possessor of a day, and this passage shows people exposed before Him on that day.\",\"limits\":\"These verses do not use the word dīn or describe the weighing of deeds.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-15:35\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Iblis’s curse lasts until يوم الدين, making that Day the fixed boundary of his allotted span and a terminus for the present cosmic conflict.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"15:35\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ ٱللَّعْنَةَ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"}],\"activation\":\"This is the same day formula as the focus, here explicitly setting the limit of a sentence.\",\"limits\":\"The verse names the curse’s endpoint without narrating Iblis’s reckoning on that day.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-15:38\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"In the same exchange, the curse runs until يوم الدين, Iblis asks for respite until people are raised, and the granted respite lasts until the known time; these deadlines may identify one endpoint.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"15:35\",\"ar\":\"إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"15:36\",\"ar\":\"فَأَنظِرْنِىٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"15:38\",\"ar\":\"إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلْوَقْتِ ٱلْمَعْلُومِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The exchange places the deadlines in sequence but does not explicitly equate the known time with the Day of Din or the day of resurrection. A clear cross-reference or exegetical identification could decide whether the endpoints coincide.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-15:87\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"If the seven oft-repeated are the Fatiha, the focus is one verse within the repeatedly given unit and carries its judgment-and-guidance dimension into recitation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"15:87\",\"ar\":\"وَلَقَدْ ءَاتَيْنَٰكَ سَبْعًۭا مِّنَ ٱلْمَثَانِى وَٱلْقُرْءَانَ ٱلْعَظِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The supplied verse does not identify the seven as the Fatiha. A Quranic cross-reference or an explicit identification from another source is needed before assigning the focus’s content to this gift.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-16:52\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The phrase وَلَهُ ٱلدِّينُ وَاصِبًا gives Allah dīn continually, while the focus names a day of dīn under His ownership; together they may frame judgment as one horizon of a lasting divine claim.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"16:52\",\"ar\":\"وَلَهُ ٱلدِّينُ وَاصِبًا\"},{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The shared noun and possessive relation are clear, but the two verses may use dīn with different senses. A dictionary or close Quranic parallel would be needed to establish continuity between them.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-17:13\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"A person’s deed is fastened to them and a book is brought out for them on Resurrection Day; this gives the focus’s Day an individual record-bearing scene.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"17:13\",\"ar\":\"وَكُلَّ إِنسَٰنٍ أَلْزَمْنَٰهُ طَٰٓئِرَهُۥ فِى عُنُقِهِۦ\"},{\"ref\":\"17:13\",\"ar\":\"وَنُخْرِجُ لَهُۥ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ كِتَٰبًۭا يَلْقَىٰهُ مَنشُورًا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names the judgment day, and the next verse in this scene has each person read their own record.\",\"limits\":\"The focus itself does not specify a written record or how it is presented.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-17:14\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The person is told to read their book, with the self sufficient as a reckoner that day; the scene makes the account personally legible and inescapable.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"17:14\",\"ar\":\"ٱقْرَأْ كِتَٰبَكَ كَفَىٰ بِنَفْسِكَ ٱلْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكَ حَسِيبًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s day of dīn is specified here through a record and the person’s own accounting.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not say that the human self replaces Allah as judge; it describes sufficiency as a witness against oneself.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:47\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"All are gathered with no one omitted, then presented before the Lord and confronted with the record in the following verses; the focus’s Day has a universal assembly before accounting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:47\",\"ar\":\"وَحَشَرْنَٰهُمْ فَلَمْ نُغَادِرْ مِنْهُمْ أَحَدًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:48\",\"ar\":\"وَعُرِضُوا۟ عَلَىٰ رَبِّكَ صَفًّۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:49\",\"ar\":\"وَوَجَدُوا۟ مَا عَمِلُوا۟ حَاضِرًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The target passage’s sequence moves from gathering to presentation and deeds found present, making the day an event for everyone.\",\"limits\":\"Verse 18:47 alone gives the gathering; the record and presentation come from its neighbors.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:49\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The book omits no small or large deed, and people find what they did present; the focus’s Day thus includes documentary accounting without omission.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:49\",\"ar\":\"لَا يُغَادِرُ صَغِيرَةًۭ وَلَا كَبِيرَةً إِلَّآ أَحْصَىٰهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:49\",\"ar\":\"وَوَجَدُوا۟ مَا عَمِلُوا۟ حَاضِرًۭا ۗ وَلَا يَظْلِمُ رَبُّكَ أَحَدًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The preceding verse presents everyone before the Lord, and this one details what the record makes present.\",\"limits\":\"The focus’s short title does not itself name a book, deeds, or the guarantee against injustice.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:105\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"People whose works were void receive no weight on Resurrection Day, linking the focus’s dīn horizon to the worth assigned to deeds.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:105\",\"ar\":\"فَحَبِطَتْ أَعْمَٰلُهُمْ فَلَا نُقِيمُ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ وَزْنًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The target couples the Day with وزن, a measure that the focus leaves implicit.\",\"limits\":\"This is the outcome for a described group and does not state the fate of every person.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-19:15\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Yahya’s blessing spans birth, death, and being raised alive; the final day can be heard as a personal life-transition as well as a day of account.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"19:15\",\"ar\":\"وَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s definite Day belongs to the same resurrection horizon named as the last of this three-part sequence.\",\"limits\":\"Yahya’s verse promises peace and does not describe weighing or judgment of deeds.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-19:33\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Isa uses the same birth-death-resurrection sequence as Yahya in 19:15; its repetition makes being raised alive a prophetic life-cycle horizon, not an isolated phrase.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"19:33\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلسَّلَٰمُ عَلَىَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدتُّ وَيَوْمَ أَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ أُبْعَثُ حَيًّۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"19:15\",\"ar\":\"وَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s Day looks toward the resurrection that both prophetic declarations name as life’s last transition.\",\"limits\":\"Neither declaration depicts the accounting that the focus’s dīn can evoke.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-20:111\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Faces are humbled before the Living, the Self-Sustaining, and the bearer of wrongdoing fails; the scene gives the focus’s sovereignty a bodily posture and an adverse outcome.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"20:111\",\"ar\":\"وَعَنَتِ ٱلْوُجُوهُ لِلْحَىِّ ٱلْقَيُّومِ\"},{\"ref\":\"20:111\",\"ar\":\"وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ حَمَلَ ظُلْمًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names Allah’s authority over the Day, and this passage depicts submission before Him within that judgment scene.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not state a weighing method or use the focus’s title.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-20:112\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The believer who does righteous deeds need not fear injustice or deprivation; this specifies the focus’s accounting horizon as fair recompense without loss.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"20:112\",\"ar\":\"وَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌۭ فَلَا يَخَافُ ظُلْمًۭا وَلَا هَضْمًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"Following the humbled faces and the failure of the unjust in 20:111, this verse states the other side of the same judgment.\",\"limits\":\"The assurance is addressed to a believer who does righteous deeds, not a full description of all outcomes.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-21:47\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Just balances are set for Resurrection Day; not even a mustard-seed’s weight is neglected, and Allah is sufficient as reckoner. This gives the focus precision, justice, and complete accounting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"21:47\",\"ar\":\"وَنَضَعُ ٱلْمَوَٰزِينَ ٱلْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"21:47\",\"ar\":\"فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌۭ شَيْـًۭٔا\"},{\"ref\":\"21:47\",\"ar\":\"وَإِن كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍۢ مِّنْ خَرْدَلٍ أَتَيْنَا بِهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"21:47\",\"ar\":\"وَكَفَىٰ بِنَا حَٰسِبِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names a Day of dīn; this verse explicitly names the Resurrection Day and what its reckoning measures.\",\"limits\":\"Its explicit scale imagery and mustard-seed example are not stated in the focus.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
